<speak>We can respect that distinction between being able to read a message and being free for a call. For routine matters, there is no need to treat a travelling client as though they are sitting in their usual office. Once your plans are firmer, you can let us know a suitable contact window through the usual channel. You do not need to give me a detailed itinerary today. It would also be sensible to avoid putting banking documents into the same travel folder as hotel bookings and restaurant reservations, simply so that your personal administration remains easy to locate when you return.</speak>